<abstract xml:lang="zh"><p>卤化物钙钛矿被视为最具前景的薄膜光伏材料之一，但其在实际工况下典型温度波动中的稳定性不足，制约了其实际应用。本研究考察了三种有机添加剂——苯乙基铵、硫脲和聚乙烯吡咯烷酮——对混合阳离子钙钛矿薄膜在 −20 至 +85 °C 之间热循环过程中降解行为的影响。薄膜采用反溶剂辅助旋涂法制备，并在 0、50、100 和 200 次循环后通过 X 射线衍射、扫描电子显微镜和光致发光光谱进行表征。在对照样品中，仅经 100 次循环即出现碘化铅相，沿晶界形成微裂纹，光致发光强度下降近一半。添加 1.5 mol% 的苯乙基铵可减缓降解：200 次循环后，仍保留初始光致发光强度的 87%，且未检测到次生相。硫脲可增大晶粒尺寸，但对耐热循环性能影响甚微；而聚乙烯吡咯烷酮可有效抑制开裂。本文提出了一种机理，将添加剂的稳定作用与表面缺陷钝化和机械应力弛豫联系起来。研究结果可为柔性太阳能组件配方的开发提供参考。</p></abstract>
<trans-abstract xml:lang="en"><p>Halide perovskites are regarded as one of the most promising materials for thin-film photovoltaics, but their practical use is held back by insufficient stability under the temperature fluctuations typical of real operating conditions. This study examines the effect of three organic additives, phenethylammonium, thiourea and polyvinylpyrrolidone, on the degradation of mixed-cation perovskite films under thermal cycling between −20 and +85 °C. Films were prepared by antisolvent-assisted spin coating and characterised by X-ray diffraction, scanning electron microscopy and photoluminescence spectroscopy after 0, 50, 100 and 200 cycles. In control samples, a lead iodide phase appears after only 100 cycles, microcracks form along grain boundaries, and photoluminescence intensity drops by almost half. Adding phenethylammonium at 1.5 mol% slows degradation: after 200 cycles, 87% of the initial photoluminescence intensity is retained and no secondary phases are detected. Thiourea increases grain size but has little effect on resistance to thermal cycling, whereas polyvinylpyrrolidone effectively suppresses cracking. A mechanism is proposed that links the stabilising effect of the additives to the passivation of surface defects and the relaxation of mechanical stress. The results can inform the development of formulations for flexible solar modules.</p></trans-abstract>
